{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QGeometricLanglands","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.PathIntegrals","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category"],"declarations":63,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.langlands_involution_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.langlands_involution_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":521,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L521-L526","doc":"The Langlands involution is an involution: `(q⁻¹)⁻¹ = q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_curvature_screening","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_curvature_screening","kind":"theorem","line":512,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L512-L519","doc":"The q-Planck constant `ℏ_q = (q−1)/q` controls the deformation\nfrom classical to quantum Langlands: the q-curvature scales as\n`F_q ~ ℏ_q · κ₀`.  At `q = 1`, `ℏ_q = 0` and the obstruction\nis screened. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_gl_classical_limit_at_substrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_gl_classical_limit_at_substrate","kind":"theorem","line":487,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L487-L508","doc":"**Classical limit**: as `q → 1`, the q-Geometric Langlands\ncorrespondence recovers the classical Beilinson–Drinfeld equivalence.\nThe degeneration proceeds through differential, Hecke, and dual\ngroup limits simultaneously.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:q-gl-classical-limit}`\nuses: `conj:q-geometric-langlands`, `def:q-local-system`,\n      `def:q-hecke-operator` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_oper_hecke_of_conjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_oper_hecke_of_conjecture","kind":"theorem","line":466,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L466-L485","doc":"**q-Opers are q-Hecke eigensheaves**: assuming the q-GL conjecture,\nevery q-oper produces an eigensheaf whose eigenvalue is determined\nby the q-oper connection.  Injectivity follows from the conjecture.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:q-oper-hecke}`\nuses: `def:q-oper`, `def:q-hecke-eigensheaf`,\n      `conj:q-geometric-langlands` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_gl_fiber_functor_of_conjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_gl_fiber_functor_of_conjecture","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L442-L464","doc":"**Fibre-functor mediation**: assuming the q-GL conjecture, the\nfibre functor `τ` determines `𝕃_q` uniquely.  The equivalence\nis forced by `FibreFunctorRigidity` + `QGeometricLanglandsConjecture`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{thm:q-gl-fiber-functor}`\nuses: `conj:q-geometric-langlands`, `rem:fibre-functor-rigidity`,\n      `def:q-hecke-eigensheaf`, `def:q-langlands-dual` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.oper_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.oper_injective","kind":"theorem","line":437,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L437-L437","doc":"Injectivity on q-opers: distinct q-opers produce distinct\neigensheaves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.recovers_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.recovers_eigenvalue","kind":"theorem","line":433,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L433-L433","doc":"The functor recovers the eigenvalue local system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.hecke_compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.hecke_compatible","kind":"theorem","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L430-L430","doc":"Hecke compatibility: the functor intertwines Hecke operators\nwith the local system action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.langlandsFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.langlandsFunctor","kind":"def","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L427-L427","doc":"The Langlands functor: eigensheaves ↦ local systems. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.mk","kind":"ctor","line":425,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L425-L425","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QGeometricLanglandsConjecture","kind":"class","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L413-L440","doc":"**q-Geometric Langlands conjecture** (axiomatized).\n\nAsserts the existence of a functor `𝕃_q` from q-Hecke eigensheaves\nto q-local systems that is:\n1. Compatible with Hecke operators\n2. Determined by the fibre functor\n3. Injective on q-opers\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{conj:q-geometric-langlands}`\nuses: `def:q-local-system`, `def:q-hecke-eigensheaf`,\n      `def:q-langlands-dual`, `def:q-flat-connection` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:q-geometric-langlands","label":"conj:q-geometric-langlands","md":"quantum-observable-universe/q-geometric-langlands/q-gl-conjecture.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_gl_kummer_filtration_arithmetic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_gl_kummer_filtration_arithmetic","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L369-L397","doc":"**q-GL Kummer filtration**: at every level `n ≥ 1`, the\nKummer divisibility criterion (`n ∣ χ` iff `χ % n = 0`) controls\nwhether the q-local system lifts through brane tower level `n`,\nAND for any `χ ≠ 0` the obstruction persists at infinitely many\nlevels (no `n ≥ 2` divides every nonzero `χ`). This packages the\narithmetic core of the Kummer filtration claim from\n`conj:q-gl-kummer-filtration`; the full categorical statement\n(level-n sublocus + restriction of `𝕃_q`) is encoded in\n`QGeometricLanglandsConjecture.recovers_eigenvalue` plus the\nKummer hypotheses below.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{conj:q-gl-kummer-filtration}`\nuses: `prop:q-gl-obstruction-calc`, `conj:q-geometric-langlands` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.kummer_no_universal_lift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.kummer_no_universal_lift","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L357-L367","doc":"**Kummer filtration — no level lifts all**: for `χ ≠ 0`, there is\nno single `n ≥ 2` that divides all nonzero integers. The perpetual\nobstruction prevents universal lifting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.kummer_divisibility_criterion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.kummer_divisibility_criterion","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L335-L355","doc":"**Kummer divisibility criterion**: `κ₀ mod n = 0` iff `n ∣ χ(A)`.\nThis is the bridge between the Kummer exact sequence in sheaf\ncohomology and the arithmetic of the Euler characteristic.\n\nWhen `n ∣ χ`, the obstruction class `κ₀` is `n`-divisible in\n`H²(S, 𝔾_m)` and the q-local system admits a lift from brane\ntower level `n` to `n+1`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:q-gl-kummer-filtration}`\nuses: `prop:q-gl-obstruction-calc`, `conj:q-geometric-langlands`,\n      `def:q-local-system` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.obstruction_cofinite_persistence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.obstruction_cofinite_persistence","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L312-L333","doc":"**Perpetual obstruction — cofinite persistence**: for any nonzero\n`χ`, the set of positive integers that do NOT divide `χ` is\ninfinite. The Yekutieli obstruction persists at cofinitely many\nKummer levels.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:q-gl-obstruction-calc}` (persistence)\nuses: `def:q-flat-connection`, `def:quantum-characteristic-classes` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.obstruction_finite_divisors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.obstruction_finite_divisors","kind":"theorem","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L295-L310","doc":"**Perpetual obstruction — finite divisor set**: for any nonzero\ninteger `χ`, the set of positive integers dividing `χ` is finite.\nThis is the arithmetic core of the perpetual obstruction: the\nKummer levels where `κ₀ mod n = 0` form a finite set, so the\nobstruction persists at density-1 levels.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:q-gl-obstruction-calc}` (arithmetic core)\nuses: `def:q-flat-connection`, `def:quantum-characteristic-classes` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_hecke_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.q_hecke_eigenvalue","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L275-L293","doc":"**q-Hecke eigenvalue determination**: the eigenvalue q-local system\n`L_q` of a q-Hecke eigensheaf is uniquely determined by the fibre\nfunctor `τ` via Tannaka–Krein reconstruction.\n\nThe proof reduces to `FibreFunctorRigidity`, which axiomatizes\nthe Tannaka–Krein theorem.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:q-hecke-eigenvalue}`\nuses: `def:q-hecke-eigensheaf`, `def:q-hecke-operator`,\n      `rem:fibre-functor-rigidity` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.FibreFunctorRigidity.eigenvalue_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.FibreFunctorRigidity.eigenvalue_unique","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L270-L270","doc":"Two q-local systems with the same substrate and the same\nholonomy residues at every point are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.FibreFunctorRigidity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.FibreFunctorRigidity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L267-L267","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.FibreFunctorRigidity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.FibreFunctorRigidity","kind":"class","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L257-L273","doc":"**Fibre-functor rigidity** (axiomatized): in a QOU the fibre functor\n`τ` is unique up to unique isomorphism (Tannaka–Krein).  Any two\nq-local systems with the same holonomy residues are equal.\n\nThis is the deep categorical input; the full proof requires\nTannaka–Krein reconstruction for quantum groups, which is not\nin Mathlib.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:fibre-functor-rigidity}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.transverse_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.transverse_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L253-L253","doc":"The transverse component is non-zero everywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.transverseComponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.transverseComponent","kind":"def","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L251-L251","doc":"Transversality: the connection is transverse to the Borel reduction.\nFor each simple root `αᵢ`, the component along `g_{−αᵢ}` is non-zero.\nEncoded as: the connection curvature has a non-zero component\nin the off-diagonal (negative root) direction at every point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.langlandsDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.langlandsDual","kind":"def","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L246-L246","doc":"The Langlands dual data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.connection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.connection","kind":"def","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L244-L244","doc":"The underlying q-flat connection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper.mk","kind":"ctor","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L242-L242","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QOper","kind":"structure","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L232-L253","doc":"**q-Oper**: a q-flat connection with a Borel reduction satisfying\nthe transversality condition.\n\nFor `Ǧ_q = SU_{q⁻¹}(2)`, a q-oper is a rank-2 q-flat bundle with\nan invariant line subbundle `L ⊂ V` such that `∇_q(L) ⊄ L ⊗ Ω¹_q`,\nequivalent to a q-Sturm–Liouville operator `∂_q² + t(z)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-oper}`\nuses: `def:q-flat-connection`, `def:q-langlands-dual` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.langlands_eigenvalue_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.langlands_eigenvalue_swap","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L223-L228","doc":"The Langlands involution swaps eigenvalues:\nthe symmetric eigenvalue `q` of `G_q` becomes the antisymmetric\neigenvalue `−q⁻¹ = −q_dual` of `Ǧ_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.langlands_dual_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.langlands_dual_pos","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L217-L221","doc":"The Langlands involution preserves positivity: `q > 0 → q⁻¹ > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.dualGroupAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.dualGroupAt","kind":"def","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L215-L215","doc":"The dual group at each point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.substrate_inverted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.substrate_inverted","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L212-L212","doc":"The substrate inversion: dual parameter is `q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.dualSubstrate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.dualSubstrate","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L210-L210","doc":"The dual substrate: `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.gaugeGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.gaugeGroup","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L208-L208","doc":"The original quantum gauge group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual.mk","kind":"ctor","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L206-L206","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLanglandsDual","kind":"structure","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L193-L215","doc":"**q-Langlands dual group**: `Ǧ_q = G_{q⁻¹}^∨`.\n\nRoot system duality composed with substrate inversion `q ↦ q⁻¹`.\nFor `G_q = SU_q(2)`: `Ǧ_q = SU_{q⁻¹}(2) ≅ SO_{q⁻¹}(3)`.\n\nThe inversion `q ↦ q⁻¹` interchanges the braiding eigenvalues\n`q ↔ −q⁻¹`, exchanging symmetric and antisymmetric channels.\nIn the `𝔾_m`-family picture this is the inversion automorphism\n`ι : 𝔾_m → 𝔾_m`, preserving torsion subgroups `μ_n`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-langlands-dual}`\nuses: `def:quantum-gauge-group`, `def:quantum-su2` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L188-L188","doc":"Factorisation: Hecke operators at distinct points commute up to the\n`O(q − 1)` correction.  At the classical point `q = 1` the\ncorrection is screened — the eigenvalue local system's q-holonomy\nresidue vanishes wherever the substrate is classical, so the Hecke\noperators commute on the nose.  This is the `q → 1` content of the\n`O(q − 1)` factorisation (replacing the former `: True`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.tensor_compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.tensor_compatible","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L181-L181","doc":"Tensor compatibility (encoded as the consistency condition on\neigenvalue data that the structure can express): the eigenvalue\n`q`-local system is defined over the same substrate parameter as\nthe `q`-Hecke operator.  This is the eigensheaf compatibility — the\n`T_{x,λ}(M) ≃ M ⊗ V_λ(L_q)_x` isomorphisms can only compose under\ntensor product (`λ + μ` = composite for `λ` and `μ`, twisted by the\nbraiding `σ_q`) when `L_q` and the Hecke action share the substrate\n`q`.  Replaces the former `: True` placeholder. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L172-L172","doc":"The eigenvalue q-local system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.heckeOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.heckeOp","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L170-L170","doc":"The q-Hecke operator data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf.mk","kind":"ctor","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L168-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeEigensheaf","kind":"structure","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L160-L189","doc":"**q-Hecke eigensheaf**: a q-D-module `M` on `Bun_{G_q}(X)` such\nthat for every q-Hecke operator `T_{x,λ}`, there is an isomorphism:\n  `T_{x,λ}(M) ≃ M ⊗ V_λ(L_q)_x`\ncompatible with tensor products and factorisation.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-hecke-eigensheaf}`\nuses: `def:q-hecke-operator`, `def:q-local-system` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.antisymmetric_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.antisymmetric_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L156-L156","doc":"The antisymmetric eigenvalue is `−q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.symmetric_eigenvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.symmetric_eigenvalue","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L154-L154","doc":"The symmetric eigenvalue is `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.q_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.q_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L152-L152","doc":"The Hecke algebra parameter equals the substrate at the base point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.basePoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.basePoint","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L150-L150","doc":"Consistency: the Hecke parameter matches the substrate at\na distinguished base point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.hecke","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L147-L147","doc":"The Hecke algebra governing the operators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.sp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.sp","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L145-L145","doc":"The substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QHeckeOperator","kind":"structure","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L132-L156","doc":"**q-Hecke operator**: an integral transform on the category of\nq-D-modules on `Bun_{G_q}(X)`, defined by the q-Hecke correspondence.\n\nThe q-Hecke operators satisfy the Hecke algebra relation:\n  `(T − q)(T + q⁻¹) = 0`\nacting with eigenvalues `q` and `−q⁻¹` on the symmetric and\nantisymmetric channels.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-hecke-operator}`\nuses: `prop:braid-action-tensor`, `def:q-local-system` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.is_q_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.is_q_flat","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L127-L127","doc":"q-flat means the connection-dependent curvature vanishes:\nall curvature is intrinsic (from the Yekutieli obstruction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.total_curvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.total_curvature","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L122-L122","doc":"The total curvature is the sum of intrinsic and connection parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.connectionCurvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.connectionCurvature","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L120-L120","doc":"The connection's total curvature `∇_q²` decomposes as\n`∇_q² = (q − 1) · F_q + F_conn` where `F_conn` is the\nconnection-dependent part.  A q-connection is q-flat when\n`F_conn = 0`, i.e. all curvature comes from the intrinsic\nobstruction `(q − 1) · F_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.curvature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.curvature","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L114-L114","doc":"The intrinsic q-curvature `F_q` at each point, determined by the\nYekutieli class: `F_q = HKR⁻¹(κ₀)`.  This is the *minimal*\ncurvature compatible with `d_q² ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.sp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.sp","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L110-L110","doc":"The substrate parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L108-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QFlatConnection","kind":"structure","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L95-L128","doc":"**q-Flat connection**: a q-connection satisfying the q-flatness\nequation `∇_q² = (q − 1) · F_q`.\n\nThe q-curvature is determined by the Yekutieli class via the\nHochschild–Kostant–Rosenberg comparison:\n  `F_q = HKR⁻¹(κ₀) ∈ HH²(U_q, Ad)`\n\nA q-flat connection has `F_q = 0`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-flat-connection}`\nuses: `def:q-local-system`, `def:categorical-q-connection`,\n      `prop:categorical-dq-squared` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Classical limit: at q = 1 the residue vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.q_monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.q_monodromy","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The q-monodromy condition: when the residue vanishes,\nmonodromy acts as the identity on the fibre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.holonomyResidue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.holonomyResidue","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L84-L84","doc":"q-monodromy residue: the `Ω_q(ρ)` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.monodromy","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L82-L82","doc":"The monodromy endomorphism acting on the fibre at each point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.fibreAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.fibreAt","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The representation type at each point (fibre of the local system). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.sp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.sp","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The underlying substrate parameter family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QGeometricLanglands.QLocalSystem","kind":"structure","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QGeometricLanglands.lean#L59-L91","doc":"**q-Local system**: a functor from the fundamental groupoid of the\nbrane curve `X` to representations of the quantum group `G_q`,\nsatisfying the q-monodromy condition.\n\nFor every contractible loop `ρ`, the monodromy is:\n  `L_q(ρ) = id + (q − 1) · Ω_q(ρ)`\nwhere `Ω_q(ρ)` is the q-holonomy residue.\n\nThe q-monodromy arises from `d_q² ≠ 0` and the Kummer reduction\nof the Yekutieli class `κ₀` controls brane tower lifting:\n`L_q` lifts from level `n` to `n+1` iff `n ∣ χ(A)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-local-system}`\nuses: `def:categorical-q-connection`, `def:substrate-parameter`,\n      `def:q-flat-connection`, `prop:categorical-dq-squared`,\n      `prop:kummer-filtration-obstruction` ","signatureChunk":0}]}